\"Coon\u201d was originally a slang term applied to white people. It described a person who was uneducated but slick, capable, tricky, and adaptable. Davy Crockett, the frontiersman, would describe himself as a \u201ccoon.\u201d Later the term gets applied to \u201cZip Coon,\u201d a stock character in the minstrel show who dressed in flashy clothes and flouted the law. \u201cAll Coons Look Alike to Me,\u201d written in 1865, introduced some elements of ragtime into vocal performance. It started a vogue for \u201ccoon songs,\u201d which carried the minstrel tradition into solo and duet performance."}],"dcterms:type":[{"type":"literal","property_id":8,"property_label":"Type","is_public":true,"@value":"songwriter"},{"type":"customvocab:2","property_id":8,"property_label":"Type","is_public":true,"@value":"Musician"}],"foaf:birthday":[{"type":"numeric:timestamp","property_id":182,"property_label":"birthday","is_public":true,"@value":"1865","@type":"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2001\/XMLSchema#gYear"}],"dcterms:dateSubmitted":[{"type":"numeric:timestamp","property_id":45,"property_label":"Date Submitted","is_public":true,"@value":"1909-05-20","@type":"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2001\/XMLSchema#date"}],"dcterms:subject":[{"type":"resource:itemset","property_id":3,"property_label":"Subject","is_public":true,"@id":"https:\/\/hearingtheamericas.org\/api\/item_sets\/68","value_resource_id":68,"value_resource_name":"item_sets","url":"\/s\/the-americas\/item-set\/68","display_title":"Minstrelsy","thumbnail_url":"\/application\/asset\/thumbnails\/audio.png?v=3.1.2","thumbnail_title":"The Whistling Coon","thumbnail_type":"audio\/mpeg"},{"type":"resource:itemset","property_id":3,"property_label":"Subject","is_public":true,"@id":"https:\/\/hearingtheamericas.org\/api\/item_sets\/631","value_resource_id":631,"value_resource_name":"item_sets","url":"\/s\/the-americas\/item-set\/631","display_title":"Ragtime","thumbnail_url":"https:\/\/hearingtheamericas.org\/files\/square\/8a5d254200cea4163cdfaba3d